    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so if we pull back the volume and intensity for a week to let the CNS recover, are we basically just waiting for the body to catch up to the previous stimulus? i'm curious how the actual mechanical side works—like, does the body just 'reset' its ability to recruit fibers, or is there more to the specific way we change the sets and reps to avoid just losing progress during the deload?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
